# Secrets for this agent. Never commit real values.
#
# The gateway reads this file at its own HERMES_HOME/.env through the home
# mount -- compose passes no credentials. That is the whole contract for
# PLOW_HOME_CHANNEL, always. PLOW_AGENT_TOKEN too, for a LEGACY-contract
# agent; a CURRENT-contract agent's own gateway truncates the token out of
# this file after first boot, at which point its durable copy is a separate
# file OUTSIDE every agent's home (`agent-mgr resolve` never prints it --
# see boot_contract.credentials_host_path in the source).

# Written in place by `agent-mgr activate`; do not fill these by hand. The
# `activate` preserves an existing canonical home across token refreshes and
# narrows the fresh token to that home's line. A home activated under the
# legacy PLOW_CHAT_* names: `agent-mgr migrate-plugin-env <name>`.
PLOW_HOME_CHANNEL=
PLOW_AGENT_TOKEN=

# Plow Latch: which Mac this agent drives, and its relay credential. Mint both
# from the Mac running Latch -- POST /v1/relay/agents needs the relay:device
# scope, which only that Mac holds -- then `agent-mgr set-latch <name>`, which
# reads them on stdin and writes them here, so the token never reaches a shell
# history or the process table. That command owns the spelling of these lines:
# `KEY=value` at column 0 is the form this tool writes and the only one it
# reads back, so an `export` or indented hand edit reads as absent.
#
# If this agent drives no Mac, delete the `latch:` block from its config.yaml
# rather than leaving these blank: the config is what declares latch, so a
# declared latch with no credential is a broken agent, not an unconfigured one.
DOMO_DEVICE_UID=
DOMO_MCP_TOKEN=
